Wes Irby wrote on 06/30/2003 11:40 PM:
> Stanislav Traykov wrote:
> 
>>What do you think, is it good strategy (probably depending on role) to
>>enchant the starting weapon/nice weapon you find and armor that will be
>>certainly not part of the AK? With uncursed scrolls before having found
>>a co-aligned altar?
> 
> 
> What would you consider a successful game? If it's getting
> through the mines and Sokoban, by all means. If ascension is
> the goal, I wouldn't use early scrolls unless I thought it
> was a matter of life and death, and you can never tell if
> that one point of AC is critical.

It's often so that by the time you know it might be critical the time 
required to read the scroll(s) will outweigh the effects..

The goal of nethack is, of course, ascending but most annoying/mildly 
stupid deaths, unpreventable by good strategy, occur before one has done 
  both Soko & the Mines. After this you should have at least several 
ways of dealing with or escaping from particularly tough situations. In 
due time you may very well turn up with spare ?oE[W|A] and/or means to 
create more than you need.

Particularly a singleweaponing character, preserving most conducts, 
should have no problems with weapon enchanting at all IME. I'm thinking 
an early +2/+3 on the weapon and perhaps +1/+2 on the armor may well 
become the difference of a successfull opening.

Stan


